## 3. Feature Specifications
### Prompt Management
#### Data Model
```typescript interface Prompt { id: string; // Unique identifier title: string; // Prompt title content: string; // Prompt content categoryId: string | null; // Associated category tags: string[]; // Associated tags createdAt: Date; // Creation timestamp updatedAt: Date; // Last update timestamp favorite: boolean; // Favorite status usageCount: number; // Number of times used lastUsed: Date | null; // Last usage timestamp }
interface Category { id: string; // Unique identifier name: string; // Category name color: string; // Display color (hex) parentId: string | null; // Parent category (for nesting) workspaceId: string; // Associated workspace }
interface Tag { id: string; // Unique identifier name: string; // Tag name color: string; // Display color (hex) workspaceId: string; // Associated workspace } ```
#### Core Functionality
1. **Create Prompt** - Form with fields for title, content, category, and tags - Rich text editor for content with Markdown support - Placeholder detection and highlighting - Auto-save functionality
2. **Edit Prompt** - Same interface as creation with pre-filled values - Version history tracking (optional feature) - Preview mode with placeholder substitution
3. **Delete Prompt** - Confirmation dialog - Optional trash/archive system for recovery
4. **Organize Prompts** - Drag-and-drop categorization - Bulk operations for multiple prompts - Sorting options (alphabetical, recent, most used)
5. **Import/Export** - Support for JSON, Markdown, and plain text formats - Batch import/export functionality - Format conversion utilities
### Placeholder System
#### Placeholder Format
Placeholders will use the format `{{placeholder_name}}` with optional default values: `{{placeholder_name:default_value}}`.
#### Detection and Processing
1. **Regex Pattern**
```javascript const placeholderRegex = /\{\{([^:}]+)(?::([^}]*))?\}\}/g; ```
2. **Extraction Function**
```typescript function extractPlaceholders(content: string): Placeholder[] { const placeholders: Placeholder[] = []; const matches = content.matchAll(placeholderRegex);
for (const match of matches) { placeholders.push({ name: match[1], defaultValue: match[2] || '', value: '', }); }
return placeholders; } ```
3. **Substitution Function**
```typescript function substitutePlaceholders(content: string, values: Record): string { return content.replace(placeholderRegex, (match, name) => { return values[name] || match; }); } ```
#### User Interface
1. **Placeholder Form Generation** - Dynamic form based on detected placeholders - Input validation based on placeholder type - Support for different input types (text, number, select)
2. **Preview Rendering** - Real-time preview with current placeholder values - Highlighting of unfilled placeholders - Toggle between raw and processed views
3. **Value Persistence** - Option to save values for future use - Context-aware suggestions based on previous inputs - Clear all/reset functionality
### Context Code Integration
#### File System Access
1. **File Selection** - File picker dialog via Electron's dialog API - Drag and drop interface for files and folders - Recent files list for quick access
2. **Processing Options** - Include full content vs. file path only - Strip comments option - Apply syntax highlighting in Markdown - Size limitation with warning for large files
3. **Integration Methods** - Insert at cursor position in prompt editor - Create special placeholder for dynamic inclusion - Append to prompt with proper formatting
#### Code Formatting
1. **Markdown Formatting**
```typescript function formatCodeForMarkdown(code: string, language: string): string { return `\`\`\`${language}\n${code}\n\`\`\``; } ```
2. **Language Detection** - Based on file extension - Fallback to plain text for unknown types - Manual override option
3. **Size Optimization** - Truncation options for large files - Compression for very large content - Warning and confirmation for files exceeding size limits
### Workspace Management
#### Workspace Model
```typescript interface Workspace { id: string; // Unique identifier name: string; // Workspace name description: string; // Workspace description createdAt: Date; // Creation timestamp updatedAt: Date; // Last update timestamp settings: WorkspaceSettings; // Workspace-specific settings }
interface WorkspaceSettings { defaultCategory: string | null; // Default category for new prompts defaultTags: string[]; // Default tags for new prompts theme: 'light' | 'dark' | 'system'; // UI theme preference shortcuts: Record; // Custom shortcut mappings // Other workspace-specific settings } ```
#### Core Functionality
1. **Workspace Creation** - Form for name, description, and initial settings - Option to clone from existing workspace - Template selection for common use cases
2. **Workspace Switching** - Dropdown or sidebar selector - Keyboard shortcut for quick switching - Visual indication of current workspace
3. **Workspace Settings** - UI for configuring workspace-specific settings - Import/export functionality - Reset to defaults option
4. **Data Isolation** - Prompts, categories, and tags scoped to workspace - Option to move/copy items between workspaces - Global items accessible across all workspaces
## 4. User Interface Design
### Main Application Window
1. **Layout** - Sidebar for navigation and workspace selection - Main content area for prompt management - Status bar for application state and shortcuts
2. **Navigation** - Tree view for categories - Tag cloud or list for tag filtering - Search bar with advanced filtering options
3. **Prompt List View** - Card or list layout with toggle option - Sort and filter controls - Preview on hover - Bulk selection and operations
4. **Prompt Editor** - Rich text editor with Markdown support - Toolbar for common formatting operations - Placeholder highlighting and management - Split view for preview
### Floating Window
1. **Activation** - Global shortcut (customizable) - System tray icon click - Optional always-on-top mode
2. **Layout** - Compact design for minimal screen space usage - Search-focused interface - Quick access to recent and favorite prompts
3. **Interaction** - Keyboard navigation for all operations - Click or Enter to select prompt - Escape to dismiss - Drag to reposition
4. **Placeholder Filling** - Inline form for required placeholders - Tab navigation between fields - Auto-focus on first field - Submit button and keyboard shortcut
## 5. Technical Implementation Details
### Electron Configuration
1. **Window Management**
```typescript // Main window configuration const createMainWindow = () => { const mainWindow = new BrowserWindow({ width: 1200, height: 800, webPreferences: { nodeIntegration: false, contextIsolation: true, preload: path.join(__dirname, 'preload.js') } });
mainWindow.loadURL(isDev ? 'http://localhost:3000' : `file://${path.join(__dirname, '../build/index.html')}`);
return mainWindow; };
// Floating window configuration const createFloatingWindow = () => { const floatingWindow = new BrowserWindow({ width: 600, height: 400, frame: false, transparent: true, alwaysOnTop: true, skipTaskbar: true, webPreferences: { nodeIntegration: false, contextIsolation: true, preload: path.join(__dirname, 'preload.js') } });
floatingWindow.loadURL(isDev ? 'http://localhost:3000/#/floating' : `file://${path.join(__dirname, '../build/index.html#floating')}`);
return floatingWindow; }; ```
2. **Global Shortcuts**
```typescript // Register global shortcut const registerGlobalShortcuts = () => { // Default shortcut, can be customized in settings const shortcut = store.get('settings.globalShortcut', 'CommandOrControl+Shift+Space');
globalShortcut.register(shortcut, () => { if (floatingWindow && !floatingWindow.isDestroyed()) { if (floatingWindow.isVisible()) { floatingWindow.hide(); } else { floatingWindow.show(); floatingWindow.focus(); } } else { createFloatingWindow(); } }); }; ```
3. **IPC Communication**
```typescript // IPC handler setup const setupIPC = () => { // Handle prompt insertion ipcMain.handle('insert-text', async (event, text) => { // Save current clipboard content const previousClipboard = clipboard.readText();
// Set new clipboard content clipboard.writeText(text);
// Simulate Ctrl+V to paste robot.keyTap('v', 'control');
// Small delay before restoring clipboard await new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(resolve, 100));
// Restore previous clipboard content clipboard.writeText(previousClipboard);
return { success: true }; });
// Handle file system operations ipcMain.handle('read-file', async (event, path) => { try { const content = await fs.promises.readFile(path, 'utf8'); return { success: true, content }; } catch (error) { return { success: false, error: error.message }; } }); }; ```
### Data Storage
1. **Storage Adapter**
```typescript // Abstract storage adapter interface StorageAdapter { get(key: string, defaultValue?: T): T; set(key: string, value: T): void; delete(key: string): void; has(key: string): boolean; clear(): void; }
// Electron store implementation class ElectronStoreAdapter implements StorageAdapter { private store: ElectronStore;
constructor(options: ElectronStore.Options) { this.store = new ElectronStore(options); }
get(key: string, defaultValue?: T): T { return this.store.get(key, defaultValue) as T; }
set(key: string, value: T): void { this.store.set(key, value); }
delete(key: string): void { this.store.delete(key); }
has(key: string): boolean { return this.store.has(key); }
clear(): void { this.store.clear(); } } ```
2. **Data Migration**
```typescript // Migration manager class MigrationManager { private storage: StorageAdapter; private migrations: Migration[];
constructor(storage: StorageAdapter, migrations: Migration[]) { this.storage = storage; this.migrations = migrations; }
async migrate(): Promise { const currentVersion = this.storage.get('version', 0); const pendingMigrations = this.migrations .filter(migration => migration.version > currentVersion) .sort((a, b) => a.version - b.version);
for (const migration of pendingMigrations) { await migration.up(this.storage); this.storage.set('version', migration.version); } } }
interface Migration { version: number; up(storage: StorageAdapter): Promise; down(storage: StorageAdapter): Promise; } ```
### React Component Architecture
1. **Component Hierarchy**
``` App ├── MainLayout │ ├── Sidebar │ │ ├── WorkspaceSelector │ │ ├── CategoryTree │ │ └── TagList │ ├── MainContent │ │ ├── PromptList │ │ │ └── PromptCard │ │ └── PromptEditor │ │ ├── RichTextEditor │ │ ├── PlaceholderManager │ │ └── FileDropzone │ └── StatusBar └── FloatingWindow ├── SearchBar ├── PromptList │ └── PromptCard └── PlaceholderForm ```
2. **State Management**
```typescript // Prompt context const PromptContext = createContext(undefined);
export const PromptProvider: React.FC<PropsWithChildren<{}>> = ({ children }) => { const [prompts, setPrompts] = useState([]); const [categories, setCategories] = useState([]); const [tags, setTags] = useState([]);
// Load data from storage useEffect(() => { const loadData = async () => { const storageService = new StorageService(); const loadedPrompts = await storageService.getPrompts(); const loadedCategories = await storageService.getCategories(); const loadedTags = await storageService.getTags();
setPrompts(loadedPrompts); setCategories(loadedCategories); setTags(loadedTags); };
loadData(); }, []);
// CRUD operations const createPrompt = async (prompt: Omit) => { const storageService = new StorageService(); const newPrompt = await storageService.createPrompt(prompt); setPrompts(prev => [...prev, newPrompt]); return newPrompt; };
// Other CRUD operations...
const value = { prompts, categories, tags, createPrompt, // Other operations... };
return (
{children}
); }; ```
## 6. Performance Considerations
### Optimization Strategies
1. **Lazy Loading** - Load prompts in batches or on-demand - Implement virtual scrolling for large lists - Defer loading of non-critical components
2. **Caching** - Cache frequently accessed prompts in memory - Implement LRU cache for recently used items - Store rendered Markdown to avoid re-parsing
3. **Debouncing and Throttling** - Debounce search input to reduce processing - Throttle expensive operations like file processing - Batch updates to storage when possible
4. **Worker Threads** - Offload heavy processing to worker threads - Use worker threads for file parsing and formatting - Implement progress indicators for long operations
### Memory Management
1. **Large File Handling** - Stream large files instead of loading entirely in memory - Implement size limits with user confirmation - Provide options for truncation or summarization
2. **Resource Cleanup** - Properly dispose of event listeners - Implement cleanup in useEffect hooks - Monitor memory usage and implement garbage collection triggers
## 7. Security Considerations
### Data Protection
1. **Local Storage Security** - Encrypt sensitive data at rest - Implement secure storage options - Provide backup and recovery mechanisms
2. **Clipboard Handling** - Preserve user clipboard content - Clear sensitive data after use - Provide clear user feedback about clipboard operations
### File System Access
1. **Sandboxing** - Restrict file system access to user-selected locations - Implement proper error handling for file operations - Validate file types and content before processing
2. **Permission Model** - Request explicit permission for file system access - Remember user preferences for frequently accessed locations - Provide clear feedback about permission status
## 8. Testing and Quality Assurance
### Testing Strategy
1. **Unit Testing** - Test individual components and utilities - Use Jest for JavaScript/TypeScript testing - Implement snapshot testing for UI components
2. **Integration Testing** - Test interactions between components - Verify IPC communication - Test data flow through the application
3. **End-to-End Testing** - Use Playwright for automated UI testing - Test key user workflows - Verify cross-platform compatibility
### Quality Metrics
1. **Code Quality** - Maintain >80% test coverage - Use ESLint and Prettier for code style - Implement pre-commit hooks for quality checks
2. **Performance Benchmarks** - Startup time < 2 seconds - Floating window activation < 200ms - Search results update < 100ms
## 9. Deployment and Distribution
### Build Process
1. **Electron Builder Configuration** - Configure builds for Windows, macOS, and Linux - Implement code signing for trusted distribution - Optimize bundle size with appropriate settings
2. **CI/CD Pipeline** - Implement GitHub Actions workflow - Automate testing and building - Generate platform-specific installers
### Update Mechanism
1. **Auto-Update Implementation** - Use electron-updater for automatic updates - Implement update notification UI - Provide release notes with each update
2. **Version Management** - Follow semantic versioning - Maintain changelog for user reference - Implement data migration for version changes
## 10. Future Considerations
### Potential Enhancements
1. **Cloud Sync** - Optional synchronization of prompts across devices - End-to-end encryption for synced data - Conflict resolution for simultaneous edits
2. **AI Integration** - Prompt suggestions based on usage patterns - Automatic categorization of prompts - Smart placeholder detection and management
3. **Collaboration Features** - Prompt sharing between users - Team workspaces for collaborative environments - Version control for shared prompts
4. **Advanced Templating** - Conditional sections in prompts - Variables and expressions - Template inheritance and composition
### Scalability Considerations
1. **Performance at Scale** - Optimizations for thousands of prompts - Efficient search and filtering for large collections - Resource usage monitoring and optimization
2. **Extensibility** - Plugin architecture for custom functionality - API for third-party integrations - User-defined scripts and automation
